Update `ExportScreen.tsx` to import `expo-file-system` and `expo-sharing` in a way that TypeScript knows the imported objects have the needed properties. A simple fix is to cast the imports to `any`:
```ts
// Inside handleExport, replace the lazy imports with:
const FileSystem: any = (await import('expo-file-system')).default;
const Sharing: any = (await import('expo-sharing')).default;
```
Then you can safely access `FileSystem.cacheDirectory`, `FileSystem.writeAsStringAsync`, and `Sharing.shareAsync` without type errors. After making these changes, run `npm run tsc` (or `npx tsc --noEmit`) to confirm that all TypeScript checks pass. Re‑run the acceptance UI flow; the "Export CSV" button should now be clickable and the export process should complete.

Apply the patch to `expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx` accordingly and ensure the project passes the static validation step.
